  "reasoning_log_text": "The study strongly supports the hierarchical processing structure (V1 -> V4 -> IT) and demonstrates that performance optimization drives models to be highly predictive of IT neural responses (r=0.87). This supports the idea that functional constraints shape representations. Predictive success is shown across hierarchical layers (HMO L1-Top) predicting IT and V4 variance. Performance optimization is key, suggesting a top-down influence on intermediate representations (V4). The study uses computational models rather than direct electrophysiology in the higher areas, limiting direct evidence for specific physiological mechanisms like SST or PV. The concept of hierarchical structure is central to the findings."
